--TEST--
a string argument at a parameter typed `property<T>|string` is offered the public properties of `T`, because the parameter takes any string and the names are the ones a key over `T` may hold — `rule:types/property-key`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class User {
    public string $email = "a@example.com";
    public int $age = 3;
}
class Grid {
    public static function sortBy(property<User>|string $column): string {
        return $column as string;
    }
}

echo Grid::sortBy("<|>");
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
age     property  int
email   property  string
